% // Cities first, and everything else second — which is the whole editorial
% // claim of the site. A reader arrives at a place, not at a topic.
< section class="index-head"
  <p class="eyebrow">{{ req.cities.length }} cities · {{ req.empires.length }} empires that held them · {{ req.ring.length }} topics they need · {{ req.images }} images, all credited
  <h1>{{ req.site.title }}
  <p>{{ req.site.description }}
  <p class="index-map">[[ See all {{ req.located }} of them on the map | {{ req.site.base }}/places/ ]]

< section class="band-head"
  <h2>The cities

< section class="browse"
  % for (const a of req.cities) {
  < article class="browse-item"
    < a href="{{ a.url }}"
      % if (a.image) {
      <img src="{{ a.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450"
      % } else {
      <div class="noimage">No free image
      % }
      <h2>{{ a.title }}
    % if (a.description) {
    <p>{{ a.description }}
    % }
    % if (a.meta) {
    <p class="browse-meta">{{ a.meta }}
    % }
  % }

< section class="band-head"
  <h2>The empires that held them
  <p class="band-note">A city changes hands. These are the states it changed hands to — each one here because a city names it as its ruler or its capital, which is a claim the city's own record makes rather than one this site invents. A city-state is filed with the cities: Ugarit and Lagash were the state.

< section class="browse ring"
  % for (const a of req.empires) {
  < article class="browse-item"
    < a href="{{ a.url }}"
      % if (a.image) {
      <img src="{{ a.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450"
      % } else {
      <div class="noimage">No free image
      % }
      <h2>{{ a.title }}
    % if (a.description) {
    <p>{{ a.description }}
    % }
  % }

< section class="band-head"
  <h2>What they need explained
  <p class="band-note">Not the subject of this site, but the vocabulary it runs on: the languages their tablets are in, the gods their temples were for, the rivers they stood on. Each one is here because an article about a place asked for it.

< section class="browse ring"
  % for (const a of req.ring) {
  < article class="browse-item"
    < a href="{{ a.url }}"
      % if (a.image) {
      <img src="{{ a.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="600" height="450"
      % } else {
      <div class="noimage">No free image
      % }
      <h2>{{ a.title }}
    % if (a.description) {
    <p>{{ a.description }}
    % }
  % }
